id=a52sxq_autofill_default
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: Google autofill as the default autofill service
author=kusti420
description=Deep dive 2026-10-16 (9.3.41, tracker L4): SettingsProvider's config_defaultAutofillService (S26U) lists Samsung Pass autofill first and GMS's credman PasswordAndPasskeyService second; the first available package wins. Samsung Pass is debloated (unica/debloat.sh), so new setups get autofill_service = PasswordAndPasskeyService, which is a credential provider and no AutofillService: AutofillManagerService logs "Bad ServiceInfo ... does not declare intent filter android.service.autofill.AutofillService" (25x per boot) and nothing autofills until the user picks a service. Stock S26U defaults to Samsung Pass. The fallback becomes GMS's real AutofillService (com.google.android.gms/.autofill.service.AutofillService, the framework's config_defaultAutofillService); the credential provider defaults are untouched. Only new setups (SettingsProvider inserts it when unset); an existing autofill_service is never changed.
